{"id":"python-factory-q1jsr.6","title":"Real FineTuningPort backend: wire actual peft LoRA/QLoRA, not the fake memory adapter","description":"FineTuningPort (ports.py) + generic LoRAConfig/FineTuningMethod (models.py) already model the agnostic PEFT surface the spec doc calls for (.github/spec/ml-dataset-generation.md: "PEFT LoRA/QLoRA... should become adapters behind the existing machine_learning fine-tuning port, do not create a separate fine_tuning brick"). But the only implementation, MemoryFineTuningAdapter, is 100% fake -- start_job hardcodes job.metrics = {"loss": 0.01} and completes instantly, no peft call, no model load. Meanwhile the only REAL peft.get_peft_model call in the brick is chronos_models.py::apply_lora, wired ad-hoc only into the Chronos time-series classifier path, bypassing FineTuningPort entirely.

Fix: add a real FineTuningPort backend (e.g. PeftFineTuningAdapter) that loads base_model (HF model id or local checkpoint per lora_config/training_config), calls real peft.get_peft_model with the generic LoRAConfig, runs training_config's loop, and reports real loss/metrics. This is the actual agnostic PEFT/LoRA/QLoRA surface -- once it exists, retire the Chronos-only apply_lora path (sibling task .5) in favor of routing through FineTuningPort like everything else should.
